# AI.32 independent-peer-jobs: QA-2 FAIL (rescoped merge-forward re-verify)
# NEW BLOCKING regression: post_commit_work.rs:265 calls canonical_home_dir instead of AI.34's canonical_graft_root
# Deterministic 4/4 test failure (tests_post_send_graft_warning) across all 3 platforms (Linux, macOS, Windows)
# PR #680, branch feature/ai32-independent-peer-jobs @ 5c6fb243

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI32-QA2-CANONICAL-ROOT-REGRESSION>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI32-QA2-CANONICAL-ROOT-REGRESSION" ;
  triage:title "AI.32 post_commit_work.rs: canonical_home_dir vs canonical_graft_root regression" ;
  triage:description "Blocking regression, reproduces identically on both feature/ai32-independent-peer-jobs (5c6fb243) and feature/ai31-async-local-admission (6063d416, AI31-QA-5): post_commit_work.rs:265 (DaemonGraftPostSendPort::deliver_post_send, introduced by AI.32 itself, inherited by AI31 via merge-forward) still calls canonical_home_dir(&member.metadata_json) instead of canonical_graft_root(&member.metadata_json). On develop, the equivalent call site (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs:101) already uses canonical_graft_root. This is a live functional regression, not just a stale test: recipients whose graft-receiver root is published via workspace_root metadata (not home_dir) will have their post-commit graft nudge resolved to the wrong path. Bisected: passes at pre-merge AI32 commit 92a722e4, fails at merged HEAD 5c6fb243/6063d416, deterministic failure in tests_post_send_graft_warning::dispatcher_send_delivers_direct_graft_nudge_without_warning ('receive graft nudge: Timeout'), CI-confirmed 4/4 across macos-latest/ubuntu-latest/windows-latest on both branches. arch-ctm's self-report that just lint and just test both passed post-merge was false. Not filed as a duplicate on AI31 — same occurrence, same file/line, same fix, covers both branches." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA-CODE-REGRESSION" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
